;;; krein-milman.scm -- extreme points, the closed convex hull and the Krein-Milman theorem in a real locally
;;; convex topological vector space (BanachAlgebras.pdf ch. 4: Prop 4.24, Remark 4.40, Cor 4.41).
;;; Agent BA-KM, 2026-11-09.  35 theorems, all modulo 0; no support, warrant, stamp or axiom.
;;; DESTINATION: theorem-library/krein-milman.scm.  Library: analysis.  Helper prefix km-.
;;; Vocabulary: structure-library/km-vocab.scm (IS-LOCALLY-CONVEX-TVS, EXTREME-POINTS, CLOSED-CONV-HULL).
;;; Load window: after structure-library/cg4-vocab (IS-EXTREME-POINT) and km-vocab; the latest cited proof
;;; files are theorem-library/tvs-alaoglu (closed-in-subspace, closed-subset-compact, subspace-of-subspace),
;;; nets (rmod-vneg-act) and tvs-geometric-hb (open-convex-positive-functional, sumset-*).  No later file cites it.
;;;
;;; Route.  Separation: an open convex v around x0 disjoint from a nonempty convex c gives, through
;;; SUMSET(v, -c) and open-convex-positive-functional, a continuous linear g with g < g(x0) on c
;;; (convex-open-separation, locally-convex-separation); hence continuous linear functionals separate points
;;; (locally-convex-separates-points).  Compactness: a chain of nonempty closed subsets of a compact Hausdorff
;;; subspace has nonempty meet (compact-chain-meet); a continuous real function attains its maximum on a nonempty
;;; compact set (compact-max-attained); the set where it is maximal is an extremal face (max-face-extremal).
;;; Zorn on the closed extremal faces ordered by reverse inclusion gives a minimal one, which is a singleton by
;;; separation of points, hence an extreme point (extreme-point-exists, extreme-points-nonempty).  Krein-Milman:
;;; were a point of ks outside the closed convex hull of its extreme points, a convex open neighbourhood of it
;;; misses the hull, a functional separates, and its maximal face on ks has an extreme point outside the hull.

